# Commit Notes

When the user asks for "commit notes", provide a plain-text summary of the changes made in the current session, formatted for copy-pasting into a commit message or changelog.

## Format

```
<Short summary line: type + what changed>

- <Bullet point explaining the change>
- <Bullet point explaining why>
- <Any relevant context (e.g. performance, trade-offs)>

File(s) changed:
- <relative path to file>
```

## Rules

- Use plain text only (no markdown formatting like bold, headers, or backticks)
- Present in a single fenced code block so the user can copy-paste easily
- Keep it concise but informative
- Start with a short summary line (e.g. "Fix: ...", "Add: ...", "Refactor: ...")
- List the files changed at the end
